Day 23 – Introduction to Advanced Java & Web Concepts

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session introduced the concept of Advanced Java and its role in developing web-based applications. The mentor explained how Advanced Java technologies extend the capabilities of Core Java to build dynamic and interactive web systems.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to Advanced Java

Advanced Java is used for web and enterprise application development.

It builds on the concepts of Core Java and provides technologies for creating dynamic web applications.

Common technologies include Servlets, JSP, and application servers.

2️⃣ Client–Server Architecture

The mentor explained how web applications work using client–server architecture.

Client → Web browser used by the user

Server → System that processes requests and sends responses

Communication happens through the internet using HTTP protocol.

3️⃣ HTTP Protocol

HTTP stands for HyperText Transfer Protocol.

It is used for communication between client and server.

A client sends an HTTP request, and the server sends an HTTP response.

4️⃣ Web Browsers and Web Servers

Web Browser → Used to access web pages (Chrome, Firefox, Edge).

Web Server → Hosts web applications and handles client requests.

Example servers include Apache Tomcat.

5️⃣ Web Technologies in Java

The mentor introduced important web technologies:

Servlets → Java programs that handle HTTP requests and responses.

JSP (Java Server Pages) → Used to create dynamic web pages.

Application Servers → Platforms used to deploy and run web applications.

🔹 Practical Exploration

Explored simple examples of web application flow.

Understood how Java processes client requests.

Observed how responses are generated and sent back to the browser.